WEBVTT

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:02.480
To the rhythm!

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:05.540
Check it!

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.040
OK, fellas!

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.940
Yeah yeah party people
let's go let's turn it up

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:33.810
Let's rush in let's send it flying
let's attack let's dash

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:37.480
The battlefields are sacred,
Bakuretsu Tenshi, Crazy Burst Angel

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:41.180
They're a bother, they're cheeky,
come on, blast 'em good!

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.560
Everybody, loosey

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.260
Be in full bloom, bluesy

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:53.600
Vividly, crazy

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.100
Fly up, angel

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.400
We are the risma so charisma

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.440
We soar, really prisma (bomber)

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:02.970
Hey! It's danceable OK
shake it right now let's go

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:05.780
Gutsiness let's go beat
let's ride the rhythm tension

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:07.410
It goes flying frustration

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:11.510
Alright let's go let's get it on
loosey beauty get your body

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:15.020
Everybody, loosey

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:18.520
Be in full bloom, bluesy

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.930
Vividly, crazy

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:25.260
Fly up, angel

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:41.180
Go, Django! Jo's waiting!

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.490
There we go, all set!

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:18.420
I'll take you...!

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:19.940
Take you to Hell!

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:37.690
Stop, Django!

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:44.760
Meg! You alive?!

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.860
Jo. Our objective is the disc.
Don't forget that.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.190
Saving Meg comes first!

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.760
Not again...!

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:13.340
Move! You're in the way!

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:15.300
Jo! Are you okay?!

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.720
Yes!

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.120
Huh? What the--

00:03:36.430 --> 00:03:40.060
Darn it! Let go, you dumb robot!

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:44.320
Oh, no, you don't!

00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:00.580
Amy! You can search from the sky!
Where'd it go?!

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:04.990
No luck. There's a
Level 5 magnetic cloud...

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:16.630
This is Meg! Sei! Respond!

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:18.230
Hello?!

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:35.050
Spill it!

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:39.220
Who do you work for,
and where did you hide Meg?!

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:43.530
I really don't know anything!

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:44.860
Don't play stupid with me!

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:54.090
No gunfire in here.
That's what we agreed on.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:55.650
I don't remember that.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.460
It seems he really is unrelated.

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:04.300
In fact, he's a victim who
got caught up in our work.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:07.600
Who in the world are you people?!

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:11.340
A secret RAPT unit?
Female Yakuza commandos?

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.440
That's it, isn't it?!

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:14.450
Jo.

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:19.550
Whatever the case, we need to identify
the robot that stole the disc.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:22.350
It's an extra request from Bailan.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:29.590
I've got a transmission from Meg!

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:32.930
She can't talk, so she e-mailed images.

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.600
You can't determine her location?

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:39.800
Nope. It's like she entered
an area that's not equipped

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:42.640
with transmission relays.

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:45.510
I'll display them in order,
so look closely.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:56.420
The downtown loop to
Kasumigaseki to Roppongi Avenue...

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:59.690
It's gone quite a long way.

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:02.490
This is the last clear picture.

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:05.850
What is that?

00:06:16.670 --> 00:06:19.110
You're helping.

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:23.210
But... I'm a victim...

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:26.020
And it's getting late;
I need to get home.

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:28.220
Plus there's tomorrow's assignment...

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:33.620
Look. Meg only got kidnapped
'cause she was trying to save you.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:36.490
It's normal to take responsibility!

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:38.320
Normal...?

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:42.960
I don't think this is normal anymore...

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:50.240
--We're not taking the van?
--Can't get there by car.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.510
--Um...
--What?

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:56.310
I'm impressed you got a gun permit...

00:06:56.310 --> 00:07:00.250
I heard the exam to get
one is really hard...

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.720
I'm guessing this bag is filled with--

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:08.280
Talk any more and I'll kill you!

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:11.650
I'm in a bad mood.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:25.070
Wait! These are the
"bad streets" of Shibuya...

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:31.820
--Let's go.
--Wait a second!

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:36.720
The government abandoned this
area after the earthquake!

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:40.390
They say that the police
can't do anything here...

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:43.160
We'll be killed if we go in here!

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:47.260
Keep shouting and I'll string
you up next to the dolls!

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:49.260
Meg is somewhere around here.

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:21.330
<i>Yikes! Everyone looks mean,
and they have guns...!</i>

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:25.340
He looked at me! Our eyes met!
Here comes someone!

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:27.440
Never seen ya before...

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:30.910
Nice bag there. What's in it?

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:35.780
Drop it and we'll let you live.

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:39.380
Nice face, but no chest.

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:43.220
You'll need at least
this much to get any work!

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:51.420
Heh! You serious?!

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:04.170
I want to talk to your boss.

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:13.440
Been a while, Miss Jo.
I was thinking of saying hello sometime.

00:09:18.520 --> 00:09:21.860
This town's a lot easier to run

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:24.660
thanks to you takin' care
of that psycho.

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:31.440
<i>You're pretty psycho yourself...!</i>

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:34.670
I want information instead of the reward.

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:38.740
Ain't nothin' in this town
I don't know about.

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:41.350
So whadya wanna know?

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:45.720
I'm looking for a big cybot
that escaped into this area.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:49.020
It's not a RAPT one. Probably military.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.860
Chasin' something that dangerous?

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:56.590
But our mics pick up
even the fanciest ones.

00:09:56.590 --> 00:10:00.730
Especially since military motors
have a unique sound.

00:10:00.730 --> 00:10:02.260
Hey!

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:10.070
It's our code not to get
involved in sticky situations.

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:15.510
We dunno about this cybot of yours,
and we ain't heard nothin'.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:17.410
That fine with you?

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:21.510
You can expect a war if you're lying.

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:30.460
She's got some guts.
Skill too. Who is she?

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:32.930
One of your relatives' kids?

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:37.870
An angel from Hell.

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:40.800
You serious? That skinny thing?!

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:44.740
She has the wings of Death on her back.

00:10:45.610 --> 00:10:50.750
Everyone who sees them
is taken to Hell.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:54.950
--You wait here.
--Eh?! By myself...?

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:57.950
Run off and I'll make Amy find you-

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:02.730
escape to South America or the Himalayas
and I'll still kill you.

00:11:02.730 --> 00:11:05.130
G-Got it...!

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:27.420
Mangle a maiden's skin, will ya...?!

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:31.350
Someone's gonna pay if I get bruises!

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:39.660
It's that red disc...

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:45.260
It's, like, pretty...

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:52.600
My cell phone!

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:03.550
I finally got the data on the place.

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:06.790
Sure was tough, though...

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:09.590
Good work. So, what is this place?

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:14.330
An underground highway
that was to be connected

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:16.830
to the downtown loop.

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:19.870
Construction stopped
after the earthquake

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:21.700
and it was basically abandoned.

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:25.210
Anyway, I know what we're dealing with.

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:29.370
An experimental robot developed
for future RAPT units.

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:33.420
--RAPT made that?
--The blueprints, anyway.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:37.450
A third party somehow acquired
them and built one first

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:39.480
by stealing the materials.

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:43.690
That related to the disc
those guys were trading?

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:48.870
No. In fact, I think they
came to steal a missing part.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:50.930
I'm checking the disc's contents.

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:54.400
It'd also be nice if you caught
them and asked them directly.

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:57.700
You're not funny.

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:12.520
No use...

00:13:35.650 --> 00:13:39.050
That was the stupid cybot's brain...!

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:50.450
Almost...!

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:56.590
Huh? Hey, don't move...!

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:11.080
I found Meg!

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:14.680
It was for only a second,
but I detected her GPS signal!

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:15.950
Where?

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:19.550
Let's see... A tunnel 500 meters ahead!

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:25.350
They advertised it would work anywhere!

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:34.400
W-What's happening?

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:41.010
Jo!

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:42.910
Outta the way, Meg!

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:53.460
Wouldn't it be best to fight
one cybot with another?!

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:55.550
Amy! You heard the lady!

00:14:57.390 --> 00:14:59.060
Roger that!

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:04.560
Django's on his way!

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:08.100
She sure is taking a while...

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:10.640
Why did she pack canned food?

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:13.110
Was she planning a lunch break?

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:16.380
What's that?!

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:20.910
--You idiot! Run!
--Wait! What about--

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:36.560
Hell's just started.

00:15:38.100 --> 00:15:40.970
Explosion detected in Shibuya, Sector A.

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:44.410
Please send a small unit to
the location immediately.

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:09.930
That's not your average cybot.

00:16:09.930 --> 00:16:13.340
It has a brain in it. A shiny one!

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:14.500
A brain?

00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:24.710
But it's more like a dinosaur.

00:16:56.950 --> 00:16:59.070
It's mad!

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:01.550
This is bad!

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:07.590
Don't stop! Run!

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:17.060
--Django!
--The party's just started!

00:17:20.070 --> 00:17:24.010
I loaded it with ultra-hard bullets,
so blast away!

00:17:24.010 --> 00:17:26.310
I found out what's on the disc!

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:28.450
It's a dump of the latest combat data

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:31.410
used in last year's
west African conflict.

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:35.720
They must've learned about the deal
and came to steal the data

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:38.780
to use the cybot's abilities
to their fullest.

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:42.830
But don't assume it's the same
as the Harumi one.

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:45.900
It should have a new OS installed!

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:48.630
Yeah. It's definitely different.

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:52.300
Jo. Recover its parts
as best as you can.

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:54.040
A request from Bailan.

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:56.010
That's a pretty tall order!

00:18:37.280 --> 00:18:40.410
Here's your leftovers!

00:18:47.920 --> 00:18:51.550
Yes! Jo's the best!

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:57.170
Got some more trouble!

00:18:57.170 --> 00:18:58.570
I'll pass!

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:14.180
This is a RAPT task force!

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:18.190
Give up your useless resistance
and do as we say!

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:21.090
I'm saved! Now I can go home!

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:23.290
--Hey!
--Wait!

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:27.890
Stop right there!
Slowly lie on the ground!

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:33.660
What?!

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:47.420
--It's Hell!
--Told ya.

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:49.920
Report from Task Force 707.

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:53.820
The cause of the explosion in
Sector A is under investigation,

00:19:53.820 --> 00:19:57.930
but we encountered a militant group
possibly involved with it.

00:19:57.930 --> 00:20:02.500
One cybot self-destructed after
engaging two unregistered Gun Cybots.

00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:05.640
Everything within a
10-meter radius was destroyed.

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:10.610
One male and one female
escaped during the confusion.

00:20:10.610 --> 00:20:12.940
Request immediate search of the city

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:16.510
and that they be taken into
custody on sight. That is all.

00:20:16.510 --> 00:20:20.280
--This is all?
--Tried my best.

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:24.720
All that and we don't know
the enemy's identity or goal,

00:20:24.720 --> 00:20:26.880
and this is all we got?

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:31.030
Grandfather's going to
give me another talking to...

00:20:31.030 --> 00:20:35.560
It's not so bad. We'll know what
the parts are once we check this!

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:40.990
Oh? What's this?!

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:47.940
"I'm sorry to have troubled you.

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:52.070
I've made you dinner
as an apology. Goodbye."

00:20:53.050 --> 00:20:55.390
He has a stronger sense of duty
than I thought.

00:20:55.390 --> 00:20:58.750
Yummy! This is super yummy!

00:21:00.260 --> 00:21:03.690
It is! Did he really make this?!

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:07.900
Looks like he has talent.

00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:10.870
I wish I could have this everyday!

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:14.100
Yes. We'll have to bring him back.

00:21:57.570 --> 00:22:05.250
I remained motionless within the crowd

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:12.890
Not even the voice of my
tears carried on this street

00:22:12.890 --> 00:22:20.600
as my feelings of lonesomeness joined it

00:22:20.600 --> 00:22:29.970
In truth, everyone wants
to smile with each other,

00:22:29.970 --> 00:22:36.510
yet they get hurt
when they can't do it very well

00:22:36.510 --> 00:22:45.520
But someone will always
be there to watch,

00:22:45.520 --> 00:22:52.720
so let's walk together
beneath this sky

00:23:13.650 --> 00:23:17.090
<i>What happened to him? Who tricked him?</i>

00:23:17.090 --> 00:23:19.850
<i>Jo's anger will dash
through the concrete jungle</i>

00:23:19.850 --> 00:23:22.090
<i>spewed out by the dark plot.</i>

00:23:22.090 --> 00:23:26.890
<i>On the next Burst Angel:</i>
"The City Where Beasts Howl"
